3 The Perpetual Session
***********************

The daemon is the durable half of ymacs (the emacsclient model).
Clients — terminal rows, GUI surfaces, headless verbs — come and go; the
daemon holds buffers, the store, and the control endpoint.  On any boot
the session is restored from the store: the open set and the active
buffer, per profile.  A ‘session.json’ from before the store existed is
imported once and then retired.


