6 Info Mode
***********

Ymacs ships an Info reader for the forked manual.  The sources live in
‘docs/emacs-manual/ymacs/’; ‘makeinfo’ builds ‘ymacs.info’, and the
installation script puts the built manual where the daemon finds it.

‘M-x info <RET>’
     Open the Ymacs manual.

   Inside the manual buffer: ‘n’ next node, ‘p’ previous node, ‘u’ up,
‘RET’ follow the menu/reference under point, ‘l’ back in the history,
‘q’ quit the manual window.  The reader follows the Emacs Info interface
so the fingers transfer; where it deliberately diverges, the divergence
ledger says so.


